// Translate in place: replace the //RS lines below with the 1:1 Jet port (keep `// Rust: <file>:<line>` anchors).
//RS //! #2517 stage S3R: the checked-body delta of one function.
//RS //!
//RS //! Body checking rewrites a function in place: it elaborates value-block
//RS //! tails, fills receiver, binding and literal types, and inserts `Ok`,
//RS //! `Place` and `Copy` wrappers. Item reuse therefore stores the parts of a
//RS //! function the checker rewrites (parameters, return type, body statements,
//RS //! reactive upgrade lines) as they were after the check, and installs them on
//RS //! a reused function instead of checking it again.
//RS //!
//RS //! The encoding is lossless for the node kinds it lists and refuses every
//RS //! other kind; a sema-filled field it does not carry must be empty. A delta is
//RS //! recorded only when applying it to the parsed function rebuilds the checked
//RS //! function exactly (`Debug` equality, see `ItemReuse::record`), so a missing
//RS //! node kind costs reuse and never changes a result.
//RS //!
//RS //! Spans are stored relative to the function's start, so they move with the
//RS //! item. Only spans the parser gave this function may be stored: a span sema
//RS //! copied from another declaration (a callee's default argument, a type from
//RS //! its signature) belongs to another item or file and would not move with
//RS //! this one, so a delta holding one is refused. The synthesized empty span at
//RS //! offset 0 is position independent and stored as it is.
//RS //!
//RS //! The same codec carries compile-time values (`encode_value`), which
//RS //! `ComptimeReuse` stores for evaluated constants.
//RS 
